+-- §49: het dossier voor de naam wordt een keuze van het artikel zelf.
+--
+-- §24 asked one question of the *soort*: "does this thing only exist inside a
+-- dossier?" (\`entry_types.case_only\`), and the archive answered two with it —
+-- where a thing may be made, and whether every list prints the dossier in front
+-- of its name. That second answer was wrong for everything else: a persoon
+-- filed in a dossier got an origin too, and so read as "Zaak Vlissingen: Jan"
+-- all over the wiki, which is not what anybody meant.
+--
+-- So the two questions are split, and the prefix moves down onto the artikel:
+--
+-- 1. entries.case_prefix — does *this* artikel wear a dossier's name? One
+--    tickbox on its own page, beside the dossier it points at (origin_case_id,
+--    unchanged). 1 ON EVERY ARTIKEL THAT SHOWS A PREFIX TODAY: the backfill is
+--    every artikel of a case_only soort, so nothing that reads "Zaak X: naam"
+--    this morning stops reading that way this afternoon.
+--
+-- 2. entry_types.prefix_default — what a *new* artikel of this soort starts
+--    with. Copied from case_only, so Clues and Voorwerpen keep the habit and
+--    everything else keeps not having it. It is a default and nothing more: the
+--    soort no longer decides anything after the moment of making.
+--
+-- entry_types.case_only itself stays, and stops being read. It is not a gate
+-- any more — every soort is makeable everywhere again — but this repo never
+-- drops a column, an old backup still restores, and the trigger below is the
+-- one thing that still asks it: on a fresh archive the seed inserts the shipped
+-- soorten *after* these migrations run, so without it Clues and Voorwerpen
+-- would be born without the default they have had since round 7.
+ALTER TABLE entries ADD COLUMN case_prefix INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 0;
+UPDATE entries SET case_prefix = 1
+  WHERE type_id IN (SELECT id FROM entry_types WHERE case_only = 1);
+
+ALTER TABLE entry_types ADD COLUMN prefix_default INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 0;
+UPDATE entry_types SET prefix_default = case_only;
+
+CREATE TRIGGER entry_types_prefix_default_from_case_only
+AFTER INSERT ON entry_types WHEN NEW.case_only = 1 AND NEW.prefix_default = 0
+BEGIN
+  UPDATE entry_types SET prefix_default = 1 WHERE id = NEW.id;
+END;
